    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple close analogues sharing the 2-methylindole-ethylamide-aryl amide scaffold show direct in vivo brain-to-plasma ratios of 0.16-0.5 and are classified as permeable or good penetrators. The closest analogue (C08, similarity 0.576) gives a B/P ratio of 0.5. The negative tetrazole analogue is less similar and structurally distinct, so it does not override the consistent positive scaffold evidence. Prediction: pass.",
